        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-[#1B3322] mb-6 border-b border-[#c9a832]/30 pb-3">
          The Mukteshwar Dilemma: Why 20 Minutes Down the Ridge Changes Everything
        </h2>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-gray-700 font-light mb-6 text-pretty">
          Mukteshwar is deservedly famous for its ancient temples and cliff edges, but staying directly in the busy commercial bazaar can feel noisy and confined during peak travel weekends. Ramgarh, nicknamed the <em>Fruit Bowl of Kumaon</em>, sits just down the ridge. It is celebrated for terraced peach, plum, and apple orchards, tall deodar trees, and a quieter mountain atmosphere that once inspired Nobel laureate Rabindranath Tagore.
        </p>

        <!-- COMPARISON TABLE -->
